Calculus, fields and differential equations for thermal models (@th-mathematics: 0, is #chapter, #part-of @thermodynamics-and-heat-transfer, #source "../sources/Differential-Equations-MIT-18-03SC.lingua#r_1VJHPM3DQ0PWYNFYKD11EKGCZE", #source "../../../chemistry/industrial-chemistry/sources/Calculus-and-Differential-Equations-OpenStax.lingua#r_027WKVM5NG5X84M86TSVRA77J3", #source "../../electromagnetism/sources/Vector-Calculus-Tong.lingua#r_2YD2PDK99N62GBWKXXCBY69PP5", #thermodynamics-and-heat-transfer "../mathematics/Exact-differentials-partial-derivatives-and-thermal-models.lingua#r_58NJQNAS8V4TVM3FAKB7HAK9QP") { r_5BYXE3KKKGPFBR1BGCVY7ZABNG
**Read:** [Differential Equations — MIT 18.03SC](../sources/Differential-Equations-MIT-18-03SC.lingua#r_1VJHPM3DQ0PWYNFYKD11EKGCZE), the complete four-unit progression during the sustained study; [Calculus and differential-equation preparation — Strang and Herman, OpenStax](../../../chemistry/industrial-chemistry/sources/Calculus-and-Differential-Equations-OpenStax.lingua#r_027WKVM5NG5X84M86TSVRA77J3), full relevant differential, integral and multivariable chapters; [Vector Calculus — David Tong](../../electromagnetism/sources/Vector-Calculus-Tong.lingua#r_2YD2PDK99N62GBWKXXCBY69PP5), complete gradient, divergence and integral-theorem developments.

A state relation, a process integral and a space/time field pose different mathematical questions. Begin with functions, slopes and accumulated changes. Derive a heated body's ordinary differential equation from its energy balance before learning solution techniques; specify the initial condition and units of every coefficient.

Work the full first-order unit of [Differential Equations — MIT 18.03SC](../sources/Differential-Equations-MIT-18-03SC.lingua#r_1VJHPM3DQ0PWYNFYKD11EKGCZE), followed by second-order equations, Fourier/Laplace methods and coupled systems as transient problems require them. Use the complete relevant calculus chapters in [Calculus and differential-equation preparation — Strang and Herman, OpenStax](../../../chemistry/industrial-chemistry/sources/Calculus-and-Differential-Equations-OpenStax.lingua#r_027WKVM5NG5X84M86TSVRA77J3) for partial derivatives, multiple integrals and constrained differentiation. [Vector Calculus — David Tong](../../electromagnetism/sources/Vector-Calculus-Tong.lingua#r_2YD2PDK99N62GBWKXXCBY69PP5) develops gradients, divergence, flux integrals and the divergence theorem used to pass between local and integral balances.

For a one-dimensional diffusion problem, derive the differential equation, initial/boundary conditions, separation of variables and eigenfunction expansion. Then reconstruct the same energy account in a finite set of cells. These are different representations of the same specified physical model, each with mathematical conditions to check. Return to these readings whenever a derivation introduces an unfamiliar operation.

**Continue:** [Exact differentials, partial derivatives and thermal models](../mathematics/Exact-differentials-partial-derivatives-and-thermal-models.lingua#r_58NJQNAS8V4TVM3FAKB7HAK9QP).

**Return:** [Thermodynamics and heat transfer](../Thermodynamics-and-heat-transfer.lingua#r_6KQBZNJM6WNV9A69R3DZY1NH7E).
} r_5BYXE3KKKGPFBR1BGCVY7ZABNG
